[Music]  all eyes are on scarlett johansson now  that black widow has finally hit  theaters and disney plus  with black widow natasha romanov has  finally got the  solo film she always deserved which  takes place between the events of 2016's  captain america civil war and  2018's avengers infinity war and while  everyone knows that natasha doesn't make  it out of avengers end game alive  black widow is still a fun ride with a  compelling story  one that also introduces a host of brand  new characters to the marvel cinematic  universe  the film's post-credit scene returns the  story to the present day where the  audience is  painfully reminded yet again that  natasha is no longer with us  as difficult as it is for marvel fans to  relive natasha's death it wasn't as  hard of a pill for johansson to swallow  the actress has been busy promoting her  new film and in an interview with bbc  radio 1  she revealed what it was like to find  out that natasha was going to meet her  demise and end game  of course when the time came to tell  scarlett johansson that black widow was  going to meet her ultimate fate  there was only one person who could make  the call johansson told radio 1 that  marvel studios president kevin feige was  the one who let her know about natasha's  fate  and she admitted he seemed kind of sad  about being the one to tell her  she said i think he was nervous to tell  me and sad about it  saying something along the lines of we  all expected that there would have to be  some big sacrifices  as far as handling the news johansson  apparently took it rather well  she recalled it didn't surprise me that  that was a choice that nat would have  made  i knew that she had to feel at peace  with that decision and that she was  doing it out of love  as gutting as it was to lose natasha an  endgame fans will have to prepare  themselves for a future without  johansen's character  as the actress has revealed she has  absolutely no plans to return to the  role in the future  in an interview with fatherly shortly  after the release of black widow  johansson delivered unsurprising yet  predictable news  that this standalone film is the last  we'll see of this beloved character  she did however hint that her  relationship with marvel is far from  over  johansen said it feels like a great way  to go out for this chapter of my marvel  identity  i would love to be able to continue to  collaborate with marvel in other ways  because i think there's just an  incredible wealth of stories there  though this may be the end of johansen's  tenure as natasha however  that doesn't mean the moniker of black  widow will necessarily be retired going  forward  as fans learned in the film's  post-credits scene yelena belova  mourning the loss of her late adopted  sister  has been driven into action by the  mysterious contessa allegra defontaine  it's entirely likely that elena will  step into natasha's shoes  and take over the mantle in future mcu  projects  natasha herself though leaves behind an  impressive legacy in the mcu  especially considering her origins  johansen herself has even recently  criticized how the character was first  treated when she arrived  in the mcu back in 2010 johansen joined  the superhero franchise in iron man 2  but after fully realizing the character  for years johansson admitted that she's  fairly unhappy with her character's  roots  describing the character's evolution  during a round table discussion with the  press johansson said  i mean you look back at iron man 2 and  while it was really fun and had a lot of  great moments in it  the character is so sexualized you know  that will be all miss freshman thank you  very much  i want one no she went on to say now  people young girls are getting a much  more positive message but it's been  incredible to be a part of that shift  and be able to come out the other side  and be a part of that old story but also  progress  evolve i think it's pretty cool check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about the  marvel cinematic universe are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

